gene-DimLightAdaptation-desc = Improves visibility in dim light by slightly brightening the field of view.
gene-ColorDiscrimination-desc = Allows subtle colour shades to be distinguished through sensitive visual receptors.
gene-Photosensitivity-desc = Heightens sensitivity to light, making bright illumination irritating to the eyes.
gene-PoorVision-desc = An inherited trait associated with impaired vision.
gene-AcuteHearing-desc = A feature of the hearing apparatus that helps natural carriers distinguish quiet sounds.
gene-OlfactorySensitivity-desc = A developed sense of smell found in animals that navigate by scent.
gene-VibrationSense-desc = Senses surface vibrations and detects movement through the vibrations it transmits.
gene-TactileWhiskers-desc = Development of sensitive whiskers used by natural carriers to feel their surroundings.
gene-FlexibleJoints-desc = Increases joint mobility, allowing limbs to bend through a wide range of motion.
gene-LimbGrip-desc = A trait of limbs adapted to gripping surfaces.
gene-VestibularBalance-desc = Helps maintain balance and quickly determine the position of the body in space.
gene-ElasticTendons-desc = Elastic tendon structure characteristic of agile animals.
gene-DenseMusculature-desc = Forms dense muscle fibres adapted to physical exertion.
gene-DenseConnectiveTissue-desc = Dense connective tissue that binds organs and supports the body.
gene-MineralizedTissue-desc = Accumulation of minerals in the body's supporting tissues.
gene-KeratinizedCovering-desc = Forms a dense keratin layer that protects the body surface from external hazards.
gene-ChitinousCovering-desc = Formation of a chitinous covering characteristic of arthropods.
gene-StructuralIridescence-desc = Iridescent colour produced by surface structure rather than pigments alone.
gene-PigmentPlasticity-desc = Regulates pigment distribution in the covering, altering colour intensity and patterns.
gene-MucusSecretion-desc = Production of mucus by the natural carrier's surface glands.
gene-SlowMetabolism-desc = Slows nutritional expenditure and substance processing. Drugs and toxins may remain active longer.
gene-HighMetabolism-desc = Accelerates substance processing and nutritional expenditure. Does not amplify every source of healing.
gene-OmnivorousDigestion-desc = Digestive traits of organisms with a mixed diet.
gene-CelluloseDigestion-desc = Traits associated with digesting fibre-rich plant food.
gene-LipidStorage-desc = Formation of fat reserves as an energy source.
gene-ProteinSecretion-desc = Production of protein secretions by specialized tissues.
gene-CellRenewal-desc = Replaces worn-out cells and maintains tissue renewal throughout the body.
gene-TissuePlasticity-desc = Tissue remodelling during growth and the closure of minor wounds. Does not replace full regeneration.
gene-VegetativeGrowth-desc = Plant tissue growth and repair dependent on available light and water.
gene-WeakImmunity-desc = An inherited trait associated with a weak immune response.
gene-ChemicalSensitivity-desc = Sensitivity to chemical irritants.
gene-XenobioticProcessing-desc = Processing of foreign substances that speeds clearance of both toxins and beneficial drugs.
gene-ToxinProduction-desc = Formation of toxic substances in the natural carrier's tissues.
gene-ToxinTolerance-desc = Tissue adaptation that reduces harmful toxin effects. Does not make the organism immune to poisoning.
gene-OxygenStorage-desc = Increases tissue oxygen reserves to allow longer intervals without breathing. Does not replace respiration.
gene-NitrogenMetabolism-desc = Biochemical traits of organisms with nitrogen-based metabolism.
gene-ColdAdaptation-desc = Helps maintain body temperature in cold environments. Does not protect against every source of cold damage.
gene-HeatAdaptation-desc = Helps maintain body temperature in hot environments. Does not provide protection from flames.
gene-LowPressureAdaptation-desc = Allows the body to tolerate thinner atmospheres. Does not protect against vacuum or replace breathing.
gene-PassiveTemperament-desc = An inherited tendency towards calm behaviour.
gene-DefensiveAggression-desc = An inherited tendency to respond aggressively to threats.
gene-StartleResponse-desc = A pronounced response to sudden stimuli in the natural carrier.
gene-FragileBones-desc = Fragile skeletal structure characteristic of the natural carrier.
gene-SilkSynthesis-desc = Periodically produces raw silk when sufficiently fed. Silk production consumes nutrients.
gene-AuditoryLearning-desc = Traits associated with remembering sounds in the natural carrier.
gene-EggLayer-desc = Allows egg laying. Producing an egg requires sufficient nutrition.
gene-Lactation-desc = Allows milk production. The milk can be collected in a container.
gene-MessyDrinker-desc = Spills some liquid when drinking. Laboratory tidiness is clearly not this organism's strength.
gene-Bleating-desc = Gives speech a distinctive bleating accent.
gene-MineralAssimilation-desc = Traits associated with mineral uptake in the natural carrier.
gene-CollectiveSignaling-desc = Inherited traits of communication between colony members.
gene-BroodDevelopment-desc = Traits associated with the development of brood offspring.
gene-NightVision-desc = Allows vision in darkness without external lighting.
gene-MechanosensoryIntegration-desc = Combines touch and vibration sensing, helping the organism perceive movement around it.
gene-NoSlip-desc = Maintains footing on slippery surfaces and prevents slipping falls.
gene-ElasticFrame-desc = Resilient supporting tissues and dense coverings work together to soften impacts and cuts. Does not increase health.
gene-LamellarScales-desc = Layered coverings scatter some incoming energy. They do not reflect projectiles on their own.
gene-CoordinatedRepair-desc = Repairs physically injured tissues while resting with sufficient nutrition. Does not heal burns.
gene-ImmuneTolerance-desc = Regulates the immune response, reducing excessive reactions to foreign substances.
gene-Venomous-desc = Injects venom during melee attacks. The venom supply is limited.
gene-DetoxifyingMetabolism-desc = Reduces toxin damage through increased tissue resistance to poisons.
gene-TorporControl-desc = Conserves nutrition and oxygen while dormant. Active exertion interrupts torpor.
gene-Pacifism-desc = Suppresses the ability to perform direct aggressive actions.
gene-ReflexDisinhibition-desc = Speeds reactions at the cost of increased susceptibility to sudden stimuli.
gene-RadionuclideSequestration-desc = Binds radionuclides entering the organism. Accumulated material must be removed; external irradiation is not fully blocked.
gene-WebSpinning-desc = Allows web spinning.
gene-ParrotSpeech-desc = Allows heard speech to be remembered and imitated.
gene-PhotonicLattice-desc = A coordinated structure of optical and protective tissues channels and scatters energy. It does not grant invisibility or reflection by itself.
gene-Regeneration-desc = Repairs physical tissue injuries even while moving, at an increased nutritional cost. Does not heal burns.
gene-ToxicOverproduction-desc = Increases venom production to dangerous levels, causing excess toxins to poison the carrier.
gene-PressureHomeostasis-desc = Protects against pressure damage. Does not supply air or protect against temperature.
gene-SensoryOverload-desc = Disrupts sensory processing, causing periodic episodes that impair movement and speech.
gene-AdaptivePigmentation-desc = Adjusts the shade and pattern of the covering to its surroundings. The organism remains visible.
gene-Radiation-desc = Turns the organism into a radiation source. Hazardous to others and requires isolation.
gene-Reflection-desc = Gives the covering a chance to reflect an energy projectile. Reflection is not guaranteed.
gene-Invisibility-desc = Gradually conceals a stationary organism. Movement disrupts the camouflage, which stops working after death.
gene-SomaticHomeostasis-desc = Coordinates repair of physical and thermal injuries at an increased nutritional cost. Does not protect against further injury.
gene-DragonBreath-name = Dragon's breath
gene-DragonBreath-desc = Allows the organism to breathe dragon fire. Does not protect the bearer from fire or heat.

gene-ThermalRepair-name = Thermal repair
gene-ThermalRepair-desc = Repairs tissue damaged by burns and extreme cold. Does not repair physical injuries or protect against further heating.

gene-CompositeCarapace-name = Composite carapace
gene-CompositeCarapace-desc = Combines resilient, keratinous and chitinous tissues to reduce blunt, slashing and piercing injuries.

gene-ThermalHomeostasis-name = Thermal homeostasis
gene-ThermalHomeostasis-desc = Coordinates heat loss and retention to tolerate hot and cold environments. Does not grant fire immunity.

gene-PhotonicEmission-name = Photonic emission
gene-PhotonicEmission-desc = Allows the organism to fire directed laser pulses with a recovery period.
